From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 09:10:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cuda/hip: let the skinny f32 GEMM take the small tail ubatch
 too (+5.6% pp534)

0044 added a wave-tiled f32 GEMM for the shapes rocBLAS under-parallelises and
guarded it with min_cols = 32. That lower bound excluded exactly the regime
where the vendor BLAS is worst: fewer columns means fewer output tiles means
fewer workgroups. 0044 fixed "few rows"; the identical pathology at "few
columns" was left in.

Every prompt longer than one physical batch ends in a short tail ubatch, and
the ranked 512-token prompt tokenises to ~534, so every single request pays
one of 22 tokens. At M = 22 the guard rejects and the matmuls fall back to
Cijk_Alik_Bljk_S_B_Bias_HA_S_SAV_UserArgs_MT64x64x16 running on grids of
**1 and 4 workgroups**.

Round-47 kernel census (rocprofv3, per pass, post-park 55-patch series),
sorted by contribution to the scored prefill SLOPE ( t(534) - t(84) ) / 451:

    kernel family                     pp84    pp300    pp534   d(534-84)  %slope
    void mul_mat_q<                  22.17    36.18    64.07     41.91    47.9%
    Cijk_..._S_B_Bias_..._SAV         0.00     0.00    11.19     11.19    12.8%
    void gated_delta_net_mc_cuda<     1.58     5.20     7.97      6.38     7.3%

The rocBLAS f32 entry runs ZERO times at pp84 and pp300 and 100 times at
pp534: it is not a scaling term, it is the tail ubatch, and it is 12.8% of
the whole prefill slope. It is also pure TTFT, since ttft = t(534).

This is a reinstatement. The identical change was submitted as 0055 in round
42 and REJECTED at perplexity 0.239% against a 0.1% gate. Round 43 then found
the series build was nondeterministic -- 25 draws of the gate command spanning
3.9269-3.9448 with ~20% outside the gate, against a bit-stable stock -- and
round 43b bisected that to patch 0008. 0008 is now parked (0055), the build
reads one repeated value again, and this change can finally be measured
honestly.

The prediction the park made testable, and the result:

  min_cols cannot fire at the gate shape. `-c 512` is exactly one ubatch of
  512, it never splits, so there is no tail and `ggml_cuda_should_use_mmf32_skinny`
  is never reached with M < 32. The gate reading must therefore be *identical*,
  not merely close.

  Runner's exact gate command, 10 loads per arm:

    stock (b10237)   3.9314  3.9314  3.9314
    min_cols=32      3.9318 x10    spread 0.000%
    min_cols=8       3.9318 x10    spread 0.000%    +0.010% vs stock

  Ten out of ten identical on both arms. 0055's 0.239% was a bad draw.

Because that shape is blind to the change on purpose, it was also checked at a
shape that DOES split with a small tail (`-c 534 -b 534 -ub 512`, ubatches
512 + 22), 3 loads per arm:

    min_cols=32   3.2323  3.2323  3.2323
    min_cols=8    3.2296  3.2296  3.2296     -> -0.0835%

Separated, reproducible on both arms, and inside 0.1%. The delta is ordinary
reassociation: the same products are summed by a different GEMM in a different
order.

Speed, llama-bench, same binary with the env toggle, 4 rounds interleaved:

    pp534  min_cols=32   3843.14  3848.95  3845.15  3853.41   mean 3847.66
    pp534  min_cols=8    4032.45  4069.53  4063.28  4083.62   mean 4062.22   +5.58%
    pp512  min_cols=32   4905.50  4867.89  4895.33  4912.21   mean 4895.23
    pp512  min_cols=8    4902.04  4896.82  4880.74  4871.65   mean 4887.81   -0.15%

4/4 separated with no overlap at pp534; pp512 flat, as the mechanism requires,
because a 512-token prompt is one ubatch and has no tail.

Lowered to 8 rather than 1 so decode-shape matvecs (M = 1) stay on the
mmvf/mmvq paths that rounds 17-53 tuned. Measured flat between 2 and 8.

GGML_F32_SKINNY_MIN_COLS=32 restores the old threshold.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmf32-skinny.cu | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmf32-skinny.cu b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmf32-skinny.cu
index cda1844ae..5e7773fc8 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmf32-skinny.cu
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmf32-skinny.cu
@@ -132,7 +132,17 @@ static int mmf32_skinny_max_rows() {
 static int mmf32_skinny_min_cols() {
     static const int v = []() {
         const char * s = getenv("GGML_F32_SKINNY_MIN_COLS");
-        return s ? atoi(s) : 32;
+        // 0044 shipped this at 32, which excluded exactly the shapes where the vendor
+        // BLAS is WORST.  Fewer columns means fewer output tiles means fewer
+        // workgroups: a 22-column tail ubatch lands rocBLAS on a 1-4 workgroup
+        // Cijk_..._S_B_Bias_... , 100 launches and 11.19 ms of a 132.96 ms pp534
+        // pass -- 12.8% of the whole scored prefill slope, and it runs zero times
+        // at pp84 and pp300 so it is entirely a tail-ubatch cost.
+        // Any prompt longer than one physical batch has such a tail, and the ranked
+        // 512-token prompt tokenises to ~534, so it has one every request.
+        // 8 rather than 1: decode-shape matvecs (M = 1) must stay on the mmvf/mmvq
+        // paths that rounds 17-53 tuned.  Measured flat between 2 and 8.
+        return s ? atoi(s) : 8;
     }();
     return v;
 }
